 has passed and it's  lost 50% of its carbon-14 we would  determine this fish fossil to be about  5730 years old but look at the insect  let's pretend the insect contains 10,000  parts per million of carbon 14  well 10,000 is half of 20,000 and 20,000  is half of 40,000 so two half-lives of  time has passed since this inside  was alive so two times 5730 years would  be eleven thousand four hundred and  sixty years that is what we would  determine this insect fossil to be look  at the trial a bite on the bottom let's  pretend it has five thousand parts per  million of carbon 14 well five thousand  is half of ten thousand and ten thousand  as half of twenty thousand and twenty  thousand is half of forty thousand so  three half-lives of time has passed so  three times five thousand seven hundred  and thirty will give you the absolute  age of the trial a bite seventeen  thousand one hundred and ninety years  old so that's a good example of how we  use isotopes to determine the absolute  age of various fossils and when we use  radiometric dating and other methods of  dating rocks and fossils we can come up  with numbers such as the earth is  four-and-a-half billion years old  prokaryotes or bacteria are three and a  half billion years old fish the first  vertebrates on earth about five hundred  and ten million years old here's the  date for amphibians reptiles mammals and  dinosaurs birds and flowering plants and  humans about two hundred thousand years  old well you know these numbers are  accurate however there's a problem can  anyone really relate to these ages you  know the average human may live 7080  years at best so it's really really hard  for a human to grasp what it means to be  five hundred and ten million years old  so here's a neat little trick that I'm  gonna go through here okay so what we're  gonna do here in this little scale here  we're gonna condense the four and a half  billion years that Earth has existed  into a single 24-hour day because that's  so